🎵 Music Store Management System (SQL Project)
📌 Project Overview

The Music Store Management System is a database-driven project designed using SQL to manage and organize music store data efficiently. This system helps in maintaining information related to music tracks, albums, artists, customers, invoices, and sales.

The project demonstrates strong understanding of relational databases, SQL queries, joins, constraints, and data analysis concepts.

🎯 Objectives
Design a structured relational database for a music store
Store and manage music-related data efficiently
Perform CRUD operations using SQL
Analyze sales and customer data using SQL queries

🗂️ Database Schema Includes
Artists
Albums
Tracks
Genres
Customers
Invoices
Invoice_Items
Employees
Each table is connected using primary keys and foreign keys to maintain data integrity.

✨ Key Features
Structured music store database design
Efficient data storage using normalization

SQL queries for:
Sales analysis
Customer behavior analysis
Best-selling tracks and albums
Revenue calculation
Use of JOINs, GROUP BY, HAVING, and subqueries

🛠️ Technologies Used
Database: MySQL / SQLite / PostgreSQL
Language: SQL
Tools: MySQL Workbench / DB Browser / pgAdmin

📂 Project Structure
Music-Store-Management-System/
│
├── music_store.sql        # Database creation & data insertion
├── queries.sql            # SQL queries for analysis
├── README.md              # Project documentation

⚙️ How to Run the Project

Install any SQL database tool (MySQL / SQLite / PostgreSQL)

Create a new database

Import the music_store.sql file

Run SQL queries using:

SELECT * FROM tracks;

Execute analysis queries from queries.sql

📊 Sample SQL Queries
Top 5 best-selling tracks
Total revenue generated
Customers with highest purchases
Genre-wise sales analysis

🚀 Learning Outcomes
Hands-on experience with relational databases
Improved SQL query writing skills
Better understanding of data relationships
Real-world database project experience

